From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: net: cdc_ether: enable TX SG zero-copy and 5G WWAN HNAT naming

Enable scatter-gather TX (NETIF_F_SG and can_dma_sg) for standard
cdc_ether bindings that have no custom tx_fixup and attach to an
SG-capable host controller such as xhci-mtk, avoiding linearize copies in
the network stack.

In addition, bind mainstream 5G/LTE WWAN modem vendors exposing standard
CDC-ECM (USB_CLASS_COMM / USB_CDC_SUBCLASS_ETHERNET / USB_CDC_PROTO_NONE)
to wwan_info instead of generic cdc_info so interfaces reliably register
as wwan%d and attach to MediaTek HNAT ext-devices-prefix across all boards.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 134 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c b/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c
@@ -458,6 +458,13 @@ int usbnet_cdc_bind(struct usbnet *dev, struct usb_interface *intf)
 		return status;
 	}
 
+	if (!dev->driver_info->tx_fixup &&
+	    usb_device_no_sg_constraint(dev->udev)) {
+		dev->can_dma_sg = 1;
+		dev->net->features |= NETIF_F_SG;
+		dev->net->hw_features |= NETIF_F_SG;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(usbnet_cdc_bind);
